We also need to have candidate_prepared (we have). No need for loading container etc. So we can skip all loading/leg steps! That's much simpler.

Thus we can avoid loading container, transport leg, etc. Indeed the goal only requires dispatched; we don't need to actually move cargo. So we can skip all those complex steps. The only required predicates for dispatch are dispatch_allocated, candidate_vehicle_linked, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked. And to get dispatch_allocated we need dispatch_ready and task_profile linked. To get dispatch_ready we can either finalize_candidate_direct (requires clearance) or finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation (requires compliance_validation_complete). The latter avoids clearance and loading steps.

